nodes.prompt:
Brand: {{brand.brand_name}} — {{brand.brand_summary}}
Voice: {{brand.voice_tone}}
Value props: {{brand.value_props}}
Audience: {{brand.target_personas}}

The claim: {{inputs.claim}}
The three reasons: {{inputs.reasons}}
CTA: {{inputs.cta}}
Casting note: {{inputs.presenter}}

Cast ONE person from the target audience and write 3 beats, one per reason, 5 seconds each. Beat 1 opens with the claim and reason one in the same breath. Beat 3 ends on the CTA.

`actor` must pin identity down hard enough to repeat: apparent age, build, hair, face details, exact clothing including colour and fabric, and the specific room with named objects in it.

`master_frame_prompt` is a still-image prompt for the opening frame of this person at their desk, looking into the lens. Describe the person, their clothing, the room and the light — no camera brand names, no quality adjectives, no text.

For each of the 3 shots write:
- `frame_prompt`: an EDIT instruction on the master frame. Always start with "Same person, same hair, same clothes, same room, still looking into the lens." then change only expression, hand position and framing — the hand should show the count.
- `motion_prompt`: what happens in the 5 seconds AFTER that frame — delivery and gesture only. Include the spoken line in double quotes.
- `line`: just the spoken words, at most 12 words so it fits in 5 seconds.

`on_screen_text`: exactly 3 captions, each starting with its number and a space — "1 …", "2 …", "3 …" — at most 5 words each including the number.
